      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also have some hesitations here. If we introduce an error, it will clearly never be reachable. Similarly, if we introduce a Response, it won\u0027t be sent to the host like its counterparts.\n\nWhat if we introduce a parent Request type called ServiceVmRequest, and the current Request type becomes an entry within it? It could look something like this:\n\n```\nenum ServiceVmRequest {\n    Processing(Request), // requests to be processed, current request \n    System(SystemRequest), // e.g. shutdown, requests to be processed by rialto, no response expected.\n}\n```\nBy doing this, we can maintain symmetry between Request and Response. Additionally, we can restrict the `process_request` API in both the host and the service VM to only handle the subtype Request.\n\nwdyt?",
